          <div class="about-paper-title">Temporal Enforcement via Mode-Separated Policy Optimization</div>
          <p class="about-paper-blurb">
            Temporal leakage lets LLMs recall post-cutoff outcomes during backtesting, so reported accuracy is often invalid. TEMPO trains temporal
            discipline with a two-mode RL objective that first drives leaked claims to zero, then optimizes prediction quality once reasoning stays
            pre-cutoff.
          </p>
          <div class="about-paper-venue">Preprint · Under review at NeurIPS 2026</div>
        </div>
