  <div class="about-research-line">
    <section class="about-story" aria-labelledby="about-story-interp">
      <h3 id="about-story-interp">Interpretation: do explanations match decisions?</h3>
      <p>
        LLMs often give fluent explanations for their predictions, but fluency is not faithfulness. The hard question is whether the factors a model
        cites actually behave like they drive the decision—and how to check that without gradients or internal access. That makes interpretation both
        practically needed for trust and scientifically interesting as a window into model behavior.
      </p>
    </section>

