            <div class="about-paper-title">Extracting Locally Linear Decision Surfaces from LLM World Models</div>
            <p class="about-paper-blurb">
              Fluent LLM explanations need not track what actually drives the prediction. LAMP treats the model’s own stated factors as coordinates
              and fits a local linear decision surface—without gradients or internal access—to test whether predictions move consistently when those
              factors change.
            </p>
